From 3c1e330aa5a41c18fca64cdf44fe41d60150e59e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Berg <gitlab@slipsprogrammor.no>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:19:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH i-g-t 01/12] tools/gputop: Guard against a zero total cycles
 delta

For drivers reporting drm-cycles/drm-total-cycles the utilisation is
computed as delta_cycles / delta_total_cycles. If the total cycles
counter did not advance between two scans that is 0 / 0, which is NaN.
NaN compares false against the 100% clamp and is then passed to
print_percentage_bar(), where ceil() of it is converted to an int. On
x86 that yields INT_MIN, which is non-zero and so ends up as an index
into the bars[] array, an out of bounds read and most likely a crash.

Treat a zero total cycles delta as zero utilisation. This also turns
the non-zero-over-zero case, which was clamped to 100%, into 0%, as a
busy count without any elapsed time is not meaningful either.

The xe driver derives total cycles from a GT timestamp which always
advances, so this is hard to hit today, but it is cheap to be safe.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: Erik Berg <gitlab@slipsprogrammor.no>
---
 tools/gputop.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/gputop.c b/tools/gputop.c
index 0ed5af456..4150309d6 100644
--- a/tools/gputop.c
+++ b/tools/gputop.c
@@ -439,8 +439,13 @@ print_client(struct igt_drm_client *c, struct igt_drm_client **prevc,
 				c->engines->capacity[i];
 			break;
 		case UTILIZATION_TYPE_TOTAL_CYCLES:
-			pct = (double)c->utilization[i].delta_cycles / c->utilization[i].delta_total_cycles * 100 /
-				c->engines->capacity[i];
+			/* Avoid NaN when the counter did not advance. */
+			if (!c->utilization[i].delta_total_cycles)
+				pct = 0.0;
+			else
+				pct = (double)c->utilization[i].delta_cycles /
+					c->utilization[i].delta_total_cycles * 100 /
+					c->engines->capacity[i];
 			break;
 		}
 
